m. I failed to actually implement `time.sleep(spam_delay)` within the loop! The input spam is running at ludicrous speed, with no delay! I see now that it should *only* trigger `Left -> X -> Right -> X` routine when a dialog is detected. It's clear I need to ensure a delay, else the process is going to be incredibly prone to errors.\n\n\n**Optimizing Battle Exit**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the overworld input problem, post-battle. My current understanding is that the game buffers inputs during the ball shake animation. Spamming `Right, X` during the ball animation will lead to unwanted overworld movement when the battle ends. The key seems to be controlling input during the post-catch screen, not blindly spamming. I see the \"caught\" message, which signifies the end of the battle, appears before/during the nickname screen. I also see that `X` is only needed when there's an overlay; the inclusion of `Left` and `Right` seems suspect and warrants further review.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat src/modes/base.py | Select-String -Pattern \\\"def _check_capture_result\\\" -Context 0,40\"","Cwd":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Brian\\\\Desktop\\\\workspace\\\\pizzant\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"2000","toolAction":"\"Reading base.py\"","toolSummary":"\"Read base.py\""}}]}
